// Basic Polygon Traversal Example
// Initializes a baseline orientation, turns angle constraints, 
// bounds a geometric square, and verifies closure automatically.

RESET
ECHO "--- Initializing Square Topology ---"

// Fixed Baseline
NE 1 5000.0000 5000.0000 "Origin"
STN 1
BS 0.0000 
TRAV ON // Active chaining mode

// Move East (90 degrees right)
AD 2 90.0000 100.000 "East_Corner"

// Move North (Instrument is facing East, turn 90 left = 270)
AD 3 270.0000 100.000 "NorthEast_Corner"

// Move West (Instrument facing North, turn 90 left = 270)
AD 4 270.0000 100.000 "NorthWest_Corner"

// Move South bounds
AD 1 270.0000 100.000 "Origin Closing"

TRAV OFF

// Outline and Draw Geometry
ECHO "--- Drawing Layout Boundaries ---"
FIGURE SQUARE_MAP
BEG SQUARE_MAP
FIG 1
FIG 2
FIG 3
FIG 4
FIG 1
END

// Validate Area and Closure Error Tolerance
CLOSURE
REPORT MAPCHECK
